# Fork / upstream safety

This repository is a **fork**. Remotes:

- `origin` → `miramocha/Extended-UniVRM` (maintained fork; only allowed push/PR target)
- `upstream` → `vrm-c/UniVRM` (upstream original; never write)

Hard rules:

- Never `git push` to `upstream` (any ref, any force flag).
- Never create a pull request targeting `vrm-c/UniVRM` or any upstream remote URL.
- Never run `gh pr create` with `--repo vrm-c/UniVRM`, or open a PR whose base repo is upstream.
- Fetch / merge / rebase **from** upstream into the fork is allowed when the user asks to sync.
- Push and PRs only to `origin`, and only when the user explicitly asks.
